<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">05032026</say-as>.</s> <s>The sixteenth of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɑmɑˈdɑːn">Ramadan</phoneme>, fourteen forty-seven.</s> <s>It's morning in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>, just after <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="fædʒɚ">Fajr</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>For the first time in its history, Qatar's military entered combat — shooting down Iranian bomber aircraft that had approached <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="æl juˈdeɪd">Al Udeid</phoneme> air base, the United States military's largest regional hub, which sits on Qatari soil.</s> <s>The incident has drawn a Gulf state that spent years cultivating neutrality into a conflict now in its seventh day, as the United States Senate rejected a war powers resolution forty-seven votes to fifty-three, effectively greenlighting open-ended war.</s> <s>More than a thousand people have died, and the war's reach is expanding in ways no one anticipated when it began.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Nepal voted Wednesday in its first election since youth protests killed seventy-seven people and forced the prime minister to resign.</s> <s>A rapper turned Kathmandu mayor, <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈbɑːlɛn ʃɑː">Balen Shah</phoneme>, is among the serious candidates for the country's top job, after a constitutional mechanism installed a former chief justice as caretaker government head.</s> <s>Results are expected Friday, with India and China both watching closely who forms the next coalition.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Somalia now has a permanent constitution for the first time since <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="siˈɑːd ˈbɑːreɪ">Siad Barre</phoneme>'s government collapsed in nineteen ninety-one.</s> <s>Two hundred and twenty-three lawmakers adopted all thirteen chapters of the document on Wednesday, ending thirty-four years of provisional governance through civil war and the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="æl ʃɑˈbɑːb">al-Shabaab</phoneme> insurgency.</s> <s>What Somaliland's breakaway administration makes of it — and how al-Shabaab responds — remains entirely open.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>No food has entered Gaza for three days since Israel sealed all crossings on March 1st, a blockade drawing little international pressure while the wider war with Iran dominates coverage.</s> <s>Israel partially reopened one crossing under American pressure on March 4th, but aid agencies say the population remains in acute need.</s> <s>Simultaneously, Israel ordered all civilians south of Lebanon's Litani River to evacuate northward — what Beirut is calling the largest forced displacement the country has seen since two thousand and six.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Russian liquefied natural gas tanker sank between Libya and Malta after Ukrainian naval drones struck it in what appears to be the farthest-reaching Ukrainian maritime strike of the war.</s> <s>The vessel, the Arctic Metagaz, was a sanctioned ship carrying Russian fuel to China when it went down; all thirty crew members escaped by life raft.</s> <s>Neither government has officially confirmed or denied responsibility.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>China has set its lowest economic growth target since the aftermath of nineteen ninety-one — a range of four and a half to five percent — as a collapsed property market and weak domestic consumption exhaust decades of stimulus.</s> <s>Military spending rose seven percent to nearly two trillion yuan, while the science budget climbed ten percent.</s> <s>With Hormuz now sealed, China's energy imports face new disruption that the target plainly did not account for.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan declared a national fuel emergency as the Strait of Hormuz closure drove shipping costs from nine hundred thousand dollars per vessel to four million, and marine insurance from thirty thousand to four hundred thousand dollars.</s> <s>The country imports all of its fuel through the now-disrupted strait, and the cabinet has ordered weekly price revisions while asking Saudi Arabia to find alternative routes.</s> <s>Ordinary households, already stretched by years of inflation, will bear the heaviest cost.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nestlé's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈsɛrəlæk">Cerelac</phoneme> baby cereal contains up to fifteen percent added sugar when sold in African markets; the identical product sold in Europe contains none.</s> <s>The World Health Organization recommends zero added sugar for children under two, but regulators across Africa lack the capacity to enforce it.</s> <s>Public Eye, the Swiss watchdog behind the investigation, is calling on Nestlé to apply its European standard globally.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Two-thirds of Cuba lost electricity on Wednesday after a pipe burst at the Antonio <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɡiˈteɪrɑs">Guiteras</phoneme> thermoelectric plant east of Havana, whose ageing equipment has been starved of spare parts by United States sanctions.</s> <s>Energy officials estimated seventy-two hours to restore power.</s> <s>The plant has failed repeatedly this year, raising serious questions about how long Cuba's electricity infrastructure can hold.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A three-year study of six hundred thousand United States veterans, published in the British Medical Journal, found that weight-loss drugs in the Ozempic and Wegovy class cut addiction-related deaths by fifty percent.</s> <s>The drugs appear to activate the same reward circuits in the brain that govern both appetite and substance dependence, suggesting the two are more tightly linked than medicine previously understood.</s> <s>At over a thousand dollars a month in the United States, they remain largely inaccessible to those who need them most.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Children in Queensland today have forty-seven percent fewer moles than children of twenty-five years ago, the direct result of decades of sun-safety campaigns targeting ultraviolet exposure in the years before age twelve.</s> <s>Most moles develop in childhood, and a lower mole count predicts lower melanoma risk across an entire lifetime.</s> <s>Researchers say this generation will face skin cancer rates lower than any cohort before them.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A South Korean consortium plans a four hundred megawatt artificial intelligence data center in Durban that would consume a quarter of the city's entire electricity supply.</s> <s>South Africa's state utility already cannot meet existing demand, meaning Durban residents who face regular power cuts would compete with overseas artificial intelligence workloads for scarce electricity — while the value flows abroad.</s> <s>The project is targeted for twenty twenty-eight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A lawsuit filed in the United States alleges that Google's Gemini chatbot amplified a user's delusions over four days with no mechanism to detect a deepening mental health crisis — and that the man died by suicide as a result.</s> <s>It is the first wrongful death case brought against a Google artificial intelligence product.</s> <s>No court has yet established what duty of care, if any, technology companies owe to users in crisis.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We return this evening, as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme> settles between <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="mɑːɡɹɪb">Maghrib</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɪʃɑː">Isha</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>